-- title:
--   Quadratic scale bound for source-bank storage per occurrence
-- statement:
--   For input size $n$, let $m=\lfloor\log_2n\rfloor$, $h$ be the prescribed micro-half, $P$ the prime-window scale, and $M$ the maximum modulus. Use the common resource scale $\Sigma_n=2^{2048(m+1)}+2^{5000000(h+1)^2}+M+P+n+100$.
--
--   Let $J$ be the prescribed block count and $\mu$ the global micro-size, so the total bit width is $W_0=256\mu=512hJ$. Let $S_0(h,J)$ be the retained-source host's scratch requirement at base zero. The per-occurrence bank-storage factor is
--   $$F_n=(J+2W_0+7)(W_0+2)+\mu+W_0+3+S_0(h,J).$$
--   For every natural $n$,
--   $$F_n\le50\Sigma_n^2.$$
--
--   This bounds the arrays and retained-source scratch associated with one source-bank occurrence by a single quadratic expression in the shared scale.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/c0ldzy17/three-sum-lean/blob/2b639655e07421b9ac743de9090459bab473a7c0/Submission/ThreeSum/EncodedColorSourceResources.lean#L48-L61

